#. translators: Main heading of the WPML Settings screen. Noun.
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. translators: The one text of the search box on the WPML Settings screen: its label, read out to screen readers, and the placeholder text inside it. Verb plus noun, imperative.
msgid "Search Settings"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Accessible label (screen readers) of the X that empties the search box on the WPML Settings screen. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Clear search"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Small tag on a search result on the WPML Settings screen; it says the result is a whole section of the settings. Noun, shown in capitals by the design.
msgid "Section"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Small tag on a search result on the WPML Settings screen; it names the section the result sits in. %s: the first word of that section's name. Shown in capitals by the design.
#, js-format
msgid "In %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Shown in place of the search results on the WPML Settings screen when nothing matches. %s: what was typed. Keep the quotation marks.
#, js-format
msgid "No settings match \"%s\""
msgstr ""

msgid "Try a different keyword or check the spelling."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Accessible label (screen readers) of the list of search results on the WPML Settings screen.
msgid "Search results"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Words for a band of the translation quality scale, at the low end: the translation has mistakes anyone would notice.
msgid "Obvious mistakes"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Words for a band of translation quality: they label the middle of the quality scale and the warning pill on the quality card. The translation is usable but its mistakes can be seen.
msgid "Mistakes visible"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Words for a band of the translation quality scale, at the high end: the translation is good enough to publish as it is.
msgid "Ready to publish"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Tag on the quality scale marking the engine the site uses now.
msgid "Your engine"
msgstr ""

#. translators: The short name of WPML's own AI translation engine, shown on its own or in bold inside a sentence. It is a product name; keep it as it is.
msgid "PTC"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Read out to screen readers in place of the quality scale. %1$s: the name of the engine the site uses, %2$d: its score, %3$s: the name of WPML's own engine, %4$d: its score.
#, js-format
msgid "Translation quality (50-100 scale): %1$s scores %2$d, %3$s scores %4$d."
msgstr ""

msgid "Scores based on WPML's internal MQM translation quality study."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Text of a link to WPML's documentation. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Learn more"
msgstr ""
